      "message": "Our requirement is to directly capture the latency of each stage for an anomalous I/O when an issue occurs: Q-\u003eG-\u003eI-\u003eD-\u003eC-\u003eendio-\u003everity.\n\n1. First, the timestamps from these stages must correspond to the same I/O operation.\n\n2. Second, we need to record this information directly, rather than first capturing a trace and then parsing it.\n\nRegarding verity_end_io: Currently, we haven\u0027t found any relevant trace at this point.\n\nRegarding endio for direct I/O: If you are referring to trace hooks like trace_f2fs_direct_IO_exit(inode, pos, count, READ, ret), they also do not meet our requirement because they cannot be correlated with the same I/O. Therefore, we added trace_android_vh_iomap_dio_bio_end_io(bio), specifically to correlate stages using the bio structure.\n\nRegarding endio for buffer I/O: The traces trace_android_vh_f2fs_read_end_io(bio) and trace_android_vh_f2fs_write_end_io(bio) were added for the same reason.\n\nRegarding z_erofs_endio: Currently, we haven\u0027t found any relevant trace at this point.",
